1
00:00:44,252 --> 00:00:47,964
DOCTOR X: MAFIA IN WHITE

2
00:00:48,048 --> 00:00:50,592
1988 GUSEO UNIVERSITY
MEDICAL SCHOOL GRADUATION CEREMONY

3
00:00:52,635 --> 00:00:54,387
Gu Bon-pyeong.

4
00:01:00,769 --> 00:01:02,312
CERTIFICATE OF COMMENDATION
GU BON-PYEONG

5
00:01:02,395 --> 00:01:03,646
GUSEO FOUNDATION CHAIRMAN'S AWARD

6
00:01:03,730 --> 00:01:06,399
Next is Bu Seung-gwon.

7
00:01:06,983 --> 00:01:08,068
Yes, sir!

8
00:01:10,612 --> 00:01:13,073
DISTINGUISHED SERVICE AWARD
BU SEUNG-GWON

9
00:01:14,449 --> 00:01:17,243
I heard Professor Min
gave all the awards to Gu Bon-pyeong,

10
00:01:17,327 --> 00:01:19,746
when they should've gone
to Bu Seung-gwon instead.

11
00:01:20,747 --> 00:01:25,335
He only agreed to it on the condition that
Seung-gwon be the one who leads the oath.

12
00:01:25,418 --> 00:01:28,296
Smart, he let
the chairman's son have all the awards,

13
00:01:28,379 --> 00:01:29,589
but as for the oath,

14
00:01:29,672 --> 00:01:32,759
he's entrusting it to someone
who really deserves it.

15
00:01:32,842 --> 00:01:33,885
That's how it should be.

16
00:01:33,968 --> 00:01:36,513
Only those truly committed
to medicine should lead the oath.

17
00:01:37,639 --> 00:01:38,640
Good work.

18
00:01:38,723 --> 00:01:39,724
Thank you, Professor.

19
00:01:40,350 --> 00:01:41,893
HIPPOCRATIC OATH

20
00:01:47,816 --> 00:01:51,903
The Hippocratic Oath. We raise our hand.

21
00:01:51,986 --> 00:01:53,655
We raise our hand.

22
00:01:53,738 --> 00:01:58,493
Repeat after me. "In my capacity
as a member of the medical profession…"

23
00:01:58,576 --> 00:02:03,206
In my full capacity
as a member of the medical profession…

24
00:02:03,289 --> 00:02:08,002
"…I solemnly pledge to consecrate my life
to the service of humanity."

25
00:02:08,086 --> 00:02:10,213
…I solemnly pledge to consecrate my life

26
00:02:10,296 --> 00:02:11,840
to the service of humanity.

27
00:02:11,923 --> 00:02:13,424
1996 GUSEO UNIVERSITY

28
00:02:13,508 --> 00:02:14,926
<i>"I will give to my teachers</i>

29
00:02:15,009 --> 00:02:17,137
<i>the respect and gratitude</i>
<i>that is their due."</i>

30
00:02:17,220 --> 00:02:19,097
<i>I will give to my teachers</i>

31
00:02:19,180 --> 00:02:21,099
<i>the respect and gratitude</i>
<i>that is their due.</i>

32
00:02:22,308 --> 00:02:24,352
<i>"I will practice my profession</i>

33
00:02:24,435 --> 00:02:26,855
<i>- with conscience and dignity."</i>
- Ready for the picture?

34
00:02:26,938 --> 00:02:30,150
<i>I will practice</i>
<i>my profession with conscience and dignity.</i>

35
00:02:30,233 --> 00:02:31,568
Yeah!

36
00:02:31,651 --> 00:02:33,820
One, two, three!

37
00:02:36,197 --> 00:02:39,242
- One, two, three!
- Nice. Wait a sec. I need to use this.

38
00:02:39,325 --> 00:02:40,952
- What about us?
- Theater club, come on!

39
00:02:41,035 --> 00:02:42,787
- I'll take the picture.
- Oh, yeah, take one of us!

40
00:02:42,871 --> 00:02:44,539
- Okay, here we go.
- One, two, three!

41
00:02:44,622 --> 00:02:46,249
- Wilderness!
- Wilderness!

42
00:02:46,958 --> 00:02:49,252
One more! One more! One, two, three!

43
00:02:49,335 --> 00:02:50,628
<i>"The health of my patient…"</i>

44
00:02:50,712 --> 00:02:54,716
<i>"The health of my patient</i>
<i>will be my first consideration."</i>

45
00:02:55,925 --> 00:02:58,845
<i>"I will respect the</i>
<i>secrets that are confided in me,</i>

46
00:02:58,928 --> 00:03:01,014
<i>even after the patient has died.</i>

47
00:03:01,097 --> 00:03:03,391
<i>I will maintain,</i>
<i>by all the means in my power,</i>

48
00:03:03,474 --> 00:03:06,227
<i>the honor and the noble traditions</i>
<i>of the medical profession."</i>

49
00:03:06,311 --> 00:03:10,023
Degree certificate, Ma Seong-gyu,
Guseo University.

50
00:03:12,192 --> 00:03:14,652
<i>"My colleagues will be</i>
<i>my sisters and my brothers."</i>

51
00:03:14,736 --> 00:03:15,737
You did it!

52
00:03:17,780 --> 00:03:21,659
<i>"I will maintain</i>
<i>the utmost respect for human life."</i>

53
00:03:21,743 --> 00:03:23,286
One, two, three.

54
00:03:23,369 --> 00:03:25,955
First, I wanna make it clear to you all

55
00:03:26,039 --> 00:03:29,375
that this decision was not made lightly.

56
00:03:29,459 --> 00:03:31,461
The negotiations have broken down.

57
00:03:31,544 --> 00:03:33,296
This is a warning to the government!

58
00:03:33,379 --> 00:03:35,131
If this issue is not resolved,

59
00:03:35,215 --> 00:03:38,051
we doctors,
led by the Korean Medical Association,

60
00:03:38,635 --> 00:03:41,221
will immediately move
to call a general strike.

61
00:03:41,888 --> 00:03:43,640
And we also want to make it clear

62
00:03:44,098 --> 00:03:48,228
that leaving our patients' sides
must be a last resort.

63
00:03:52,899 --> 00:03:55,777
2026 PRESS CONFERENCE
MEDICAL SCHOOL QUOTA INCREASE OPPOSITION

64
00:03:55,860 --> 00:03:57,779
Hello, I am Ma Seong-gyu,

65
00:03:57,862 --> 00:04:01,241
head of the Gyeonggi-do branch
of the Korean Intern Resident Association.

66
00:04:02,033 --> 00:04:05,370
We have decided that in 42 hours,
at 6 a.m. this Wednesday,

67
00:04:05,954 --> 00:04:09,457
all interns are to stop the execution
of their duties and exit the hospital…

68
00:04:10,166 --> 00:04:12,460
<i>"I will not permit considerations</i>

69
00:04:12,543 --> 00:04:14,045
<i>of age, disease or disability,</i>

70
00:04:14,128 --> 00:04:16,589
<i>creed, ethnic origin, gender, nationality,</i>

71
00:04:16,673 --> 00:04:21,219
<i>political affiliation, race,</i>
<i>sexual orientation, social standing</i>

72
00:04:21,302 --> 00:04:25,598
<i>or any other factor to intervene</i>
<i>between my duty and my patient.</i>

73
00:04:25,682 --> 00:04:30,561
<i>I will not use my medical knowledge</i>
<i>contrary to the laws of humanity,</i>

74
00:04:30,645 --> 00:04:32,063
<i>even under threat."</i>

75
00:04:40,196 --> 00:04:44,367
<i>"I make these promises solemnly,</i>

76
00:04:44,450 --> 00:04:48,496
<i>freely, and upon my honor."</i>

77
00:05:07,432 --> 00:05:10,935
DOCTOR X: MAFIA IN WHITE

78
00:05:16,733 --> 00:05:18,860
EPISODE 8

79
00:05:29,203 --> 00:05:32,123
42 HOURS BEFORE WORK STOPPAGE

80
00:05:32,874 --> 00:05:34,459
I can't see the cut surface properly.

81
00:05:34,542 --> 00:05:35,668
I'll place a retractor.

82
00:05:35,752 --> 00:05:37,503
- Place one on the other side too.
- Yes, Dr. Gye.

83
00:05:37,587 --> 00:05:38,921
Vitals are unstable.

84
00:05:43,551 --> 00:05:44,677
Damn it.

85
00:05:45,386 --> 00:05:48,222
Like a teddy bear has any vitals. Geez.

86
00:05:48,806 --> 00:05:51,100
That damn theater geek.

87
00:05:51,184 --> 00:05:52,018
You got this!

88
00:05:52,602 --> 00:05:55,480
- "You got this"?
- "You got this," my ass.

89
00:05:55,563 --> 00:05:57,190
Way to go! You got it!

90
00:05:59,484 --> 00:06:00,360
I don't do that.

91
00:06:02,528 --> 00:06:04,822
You won't even think about it?

92
00:06:04,906 --> 00:06:06,199
What kind of monster are you?

93
00:06:06,783 --> 00:06:09,077
You of all people, Dr. Gye,
the mad dog of the OR,

94
00:06:09,160 --> 00:06:10,745
you're refusing to perform surgery?

95
00:06:10,828 --> 00:06:12,830
This isn't surgery--

96
00:06:12,914 --> 00:06:14,374
Please, just do the surgery.

97
00:06:14,457 --> 00:06:15,708
Look, his family is crying.

98
00:06:15,792 --> 00:06:17,335
Why do you keep calling me over when--

99
00:06:17,418 --> 00:06:18,544
What is this?

100
00:06:18,628 --> 00:06:20,004
It's ripped to shreds,
you should throw it out--

101
00:06:20,088 --> 00:06:21,839
Hey, hey, hey.
Don't contaminate the patient.

102
00:06:21,923 --> 00:06:23,674
Be quiet, she can hear you.

103
00:06:23,758 --> 00:06:24,592
I'm gonna go.

104
00:06:24,675 --> 00:06:26,302
- No, no. No, no.
- Me too.

105
00:06:26,386 --> 00:06:29,222
Just, uh, open up an OR. Please, hurry.

106
00:06:29,305 --> 00:06:30,640
This is nonsense. Let me go.

107
00:06:30,723 --> 00:06:35,144
Doctor, will my Snuggles
be able to get surgery?

108
00:06:35,228 --> 00:06:38,898
Oh! Of course, Hyeon-a. Of course.

109
00:06:39,524 --> 00:06:43,111
Oh, I would like you to meet
Dr. Gye Su-jeong.

110
00:06:43,194 --> 00:06:45,947
Wow, Dr. Gye Su-jeong.

111
00:06:47,198 --> 00:06:48,116
You know me?

112
00:06:49,450 --> 00:06:51,619
Some of the doctors in my ward
were talking about you

113
00:06:51,702 --> 00:06:55,873
and they said that you were the best
surgeon that they had at the hospital.

114
00:06:56,707 --> 00:06:59,627
Dr. Kim said you're
an amazing doctor, as well.

115
00:07:01,712 --> 00:07:02,839
Your ward?

116
00:07:03,506 --> 00:07:05,758
Ah, Hyeon-a, you're really smart.

117
00:07:05,842 --> 00:07:09,178
How'd you know to bring Snuggles
to the ER when she got hurt?

118
00:07:09,262 --> 00:07:11,889
Sometimes I collapse at home
after I leave here.

119
00:07:11,973 --> 00:07:14,559
- I see.
- When that happens, I come back.

120
00:07:15,268 --> 00:07:17,228
So I thought my Snuggles should too.

121
00:07:18,771 --> 00:07:21,524
Oh, this is Lee Hyeon-a.
Eight year old, and she's my friend.

122
00:07:21,607 --> 00:07:22,442
Right?

123
00:07:23,025 --> 00:07:24,861
Hyeon-a is so brave, you know?

124
00:07:24,944 --> 00:07:26,612
Even if it hurts a lot,

125
00:07:26,696 --> 00:07:30,241
she still tells us her name and where
it hurts, so we know. Doesn't she?

126
00:07:30,324 --> 00:07:33,744
Wow. A lot of grown-ups can't do that.

127
00:07:33,828 --> 00:07:34,871
It's so good that you can.

128
00:07:36,080 --> 00:07:37,290
Dr. Gye Su-jeong.

129
00:07:38,374 --> 00:07:41,335
Will Snuggles live if she gets surgery?

130
00:07:43,588 --> 00:07:46,382
When you say "live,"

131
00:07:46,466 --> 00:07:50,678
I don't really know exactly what you mean.

132
00:07:51,220 --> 00:07:53,264
Why don't you just get a new one--

133
00:08:07,069 --> 00:08:10,615
Ah! Ah! Name, Lee Snuggles, six years old.

134
00:08:10,698 --> 00:08:12,700
Deep lacerations on the patient's--

135
00:08:12,783 --> 00:08:14,577
We'll deal with the organ injury first,

136
00:08:14,660 --> 00:08:15,995
then the lacerations.

137
00:08:16,078 --> 00:08:17,205
Okay, message understood.

138
00:08:17,288 --> 00:08:19,874
I just wanted to try this once.
Over and out.

139
00:08:22,502 --> 00:08:24,420
Hyeon-a, so cool, isn't it?

140
00:08:26,214 --> 00:08:29,383
Man, I swear I'll make him pay for this.

141
00:08:30,426 --> 00:08:32,345
So, do I just play along like…

142
00:08:32,970 --> 00:08:35,598
Vitals… …are stable now.

143
00:08:35,681 --> 00:08:36,807
Got it.

144
00:08:36,891 --> 00:08:39,310
Dr. Gye, you have to take this seriously.

145
00:08:39,393 --> 00:08:40,853
Hyeon-a is watching.

146
00:08:44,774 --> 00:08:47,818
Dr. Kim got us a lot of new stuffing,
so let's make Snuggles cuddly again.

147
00:08:47,902 --> 00:08:49,654
We'll make her nice and plump,
pack it in tight--

148
00:08:49,737 --> 00:08:52,114
- I'll pack this in your mouth.
- Closing up now.

149
00:08:59,497 --> 00:09:00,790
Be careful on that.

150
00:09:00,873 --> 00:09:03,209
- I will!
- I'm always careful.

151
00:09:04,126 --> 00:09:06,420
Okay, you guys, who wants to play?

152
00:09:06,504 --> 00:09:07,797
- I do!
- I do too!

153
00:09:07,880 --> 00:09:10,633
This… is "snow."

154
00:09:11,259 --> 00:09:12,218
Can you say that?

155
00:09:12,802 --> 00:09:14,053
- "Snow."
- Snow.

156
00:09:14,136 --> 00:09:15,221
"Snow."

157
00:09:15,304 --> 00:09:16,806
- Time to go in.
- "Snow."

158
00:09:16,889 --> 00:09:18,766
- Okay, guys.
- I want to see snow.

159
00:09:19,976 --> 00:09:22,395
We'll take you there with us
before the end of the year.

160
00:09:23,062 --> 00:09:23,938
Both Baraka and Neema.

161
00:09:25,982 --> 00:09:28,234
Push me!

162
00:09:28,317 --> 00:09:30,319
Hey, look. Here it is.

163
00:09:30,403 --> 00:09:33,781
Use this to rip it out.

164
00:09:37,034 --> 00:09:37,868
Neema.

165
00:09:39,328 --> 00:09:40,162
Yes.

166
00:09:40,955 --> 00:09:42,248
This is your hand.

167
00:09:42,331 --> 00:09:44,417
- Hand.
- Can you say it too?

168
00:09:44,500 --> 00:09:46,127
- Hand. Hand.
- Good.

169
00:09:46,210 --> 00:09:49,005
And this is your heart.

170
00:09:49,088 --> 00:09:50,590
"Heart."

171
00:09:50,673 --> 00:09:51,966
- Heart.
- Heart.

172
00:09:52,049 --> 00:09:52,883
"Heart."

173
00:09:52,967 --> 00:09:54,260
- Heart.
- "Heart."

174
00:09:54,343 --> 00:09:55,928
- "Heart."
- What's a heart?

175
00:09:56,012 --> 00:09:59,140
Uh, well… hmm…

176
00:10:01,183 --> 00:10:02,435
"My soul."

177
00:10:02,518 --> 00:10:04,395
My soul.

178
00:10:04,478 --> 00:10:07,356
- My soul.
- Yes. "My soul."

179
00:10:07,440 --> 00:10:09,567
- My soul.
- Perfect.

180
00:10:11,068 --> 00:10:14,697
And boom! Dolly!

181
00:10:16,073 --> 00:10:18,701
- Neema!
- Wow!

182
00:10:43,643 --> 00:10:46,520
LEE SNUGGLES, F/6

183
00:10:48,898 --> 00:10:49,899
Cut.

184
00:10:49,982 --> 00:10:50,941
BLOOD PRESSURE CUFF

185
00:10:51,025 --> 00:10:52,902
Oh, I think they're done.

186
00:11:02,578 --> 00:11:05,665
Hyeon-a, the surgery is over.
It was a success.

187
00:11:34,068 --> 00:11:35,986
<i>She has malignant myofibroblastoma.</i>

188
00:11:36,570 --> 00:11:38,155
Thank you.

189
00:11:38,781 --> 00:11:42,451
<i>It's 15 cm and wrapped around</i>
<i>her entire abdomen.</i>

190
00:11:42,535 --> 00:11:45,121
<i>Palliative chemo is all we can do now.</i>

191
00:11:45,621 --> 00:11:48,040
- Mom, wait a second.
- Hmm?

192
00:11:58,050 --> 00:12:01,929
<i>She knows that no one can operate on her.</i>

193
00:12:06,183 --> 00:12:11,522
Dr. Gye. Thank you so much.
And if I end up leaving this world,

194
00:12:12,148 --> 00:12:15,484
would you please take care
of my Snuggles for me, if you could?

195
00:12:16,694 --> 00:12:19,238
And if… if she ever gets sick again,

196
00:12:19,321 --> 00:12:21,741
I only want you to operate on her.

197
00:12:26,203 --> 00:12:30,207
Oh, and don't tell my mom.
Can you just keep it as a secret?

198
00:12:46,390 --> 00:12:47,600
Hey, Hyeon-a.

199
00:12:47,683 --> 00:12:50,436
You know, Snuggles
got her surgery thanks to me,

200
00:12:50,519 --> 00:12:52,772
so you have to come visit me again, okay?

201
00:12:52,855 --> 00:12:56,108
The gummies I eat while talking to you
are the best tasting.

202
00:12:56,901 --> 00:12:59,904
These are yours. Just remember,
they're only for you, okay?

203
00:13:04,283 --> 00:13:05,284
Very good.

204
00:13:11,081 --> 00:13:12,082
Don't run. Don't run.

205
00:13:14,502 --> 00:13:16,545
GUSEO UNIVERSITY CHILDREN'S HOSPITAL
MAKING CHILDREN HAPPY

206
00:13:20,216 --> 00:13:21,258
I gave her a hug.

207
00:13:26,263 --> 00:13:29,475
Dr. Gye,
you know your phone keeps ringing.

208
00:13:33,270 --> 00:13:38,234
I heard Dr. Gye Su-jeong finally has
a desk of her own in the staff room now.

209
00:13:39,068 --> 00:13:40,319
Yes, well…

210
00:13:41,070 --> 00:13:43,072
There were an array of circumstances.

211
00:13:43,906 --> 00:13:46,909
Dr. Gye, are you happy with your desk?

212
00:13:52,623 --> 00:13:54,333
I haven't even sat at it yet.

213
00:13:54,416 --> 00:13:57,837
Oh, well, that's because
you're always in surgery, aren't you?

214
00:13:58,420 --> 00:14:01,632
Well, between
Mr. Oh Sang-beom and everything else,

215
00:14:01,715 --> 00:14:04,593
I'll admit that Dr. Gye
has proved herself to be very helpful.

216
00:14:04,677 --> 00:14:07,763
Well, hearing that makes me happy.

217
00:14:07,847 --> 00:14:09,932
Should we throw a desk-warming party?

218
00:14:10,015 --> 00:14:12,142
Uh…

219
00:14:12,226 --> 00:14:14,311
Although you don't look very pleased.

220
00:14:15,104 --> 00:14:18,190
Oh, aren't you Dr. Jang Gil-yeong
from neurosurgery?

221
00:14:18,274 --> 00:14:21,443
Yes. How did you know?

222
00:14:21,527 --> 00:14:23,821
I see you haven't quit yet.

223
00:14:23,904 --> 00:14:27,157
Uh-huh, I haven't quit yet and I refuse!
I'm still here!

224
00:14:27,241 --> 00:14:31,829
What are you going to make…
make me quit right now?

225
00:14:31,912 --> 00:14:34,206
Dr. Jang, calm down.

226
00:14:35,165 --> 00:14:37,751
It's just a joke, a joke.

227
00:14:37,835 --> 00:14:39,420
Of course I recognize you.

228
00:14:39,503 --> 00:14:41,547
You're one of the country's
best neurosurgeons

229
00:14:41,630 --> 00:14:42,715
when it comes to craniotomies.

230
00:14:42,798 --> 00:14:45,384
What difference does it make?
He's never even around.

231
00:14:45,467 --> 00:14:47,136
Hey look, back then, I had to--

232
00:14:47,219 --> 00:14:50,723
Obviously, you're never around because
you're always in the operating room,

233
00:14:50,806 --> 00:14:53,183
and you've been even busier lately.

234
00:14:53,684 --> 00:14:56,645
Uh, so, uh, moving forward,

235
00:14:56,729 --> 00:15:01,108
she can take on some neurosurgery cases
as well as some consultations.

236
00:15:01,191 --> 00:15:02,860
Oh, of course, of course.

237
00:15:02,943 --> 00:15:05,905
Absolutely, she's happy to help out
as much as she possibly can.

238
00:15:05,988 --> 00:15:08,115
Just don't neglect your GS duties, got it?

239
00:15:08,198 --> 00:15:09,867
Oh, of course not.

240
00:15:10,451 --> 00:15:13,913
But I think it's in situations like this
that Dr. Gye works best

241
00:15:13,996 --> 00:15:16,040
and can fully utilize her super power.

242
00:15:16,790 --> 00:15:19,043
She's kind of like a jack-of-all-trades.

243
00:15:19,752 --> 00:15:22,630
So, any other specialties
you wanna tell us about while you're here?

244
00:15:22,713 --> 00:15:24,506
In case of anything unexpected.

245
00:15:24,590 --> 00:15:26,216
Right, and on that note…

246
00:15:27,635 --> 00:15:29,678
We have a new contract.

247
00:15:30,179 --> 00:15:31,305
Here.

248
00:15:34,725 --> 00:15:37,770
In light of the current situation
regarding shortages of medical staff,

249
00:15:37,853 --> 00:15:42,232
we would like you to offer
a tiny token of your appreciation.

250
00:15:42,733 --> 00:15:44,860
So you're gonna gouge us now, huh?

251
00:15:44,944 --> 00:15:48,614
Go ahead, take us for a ride, it's okay.
Everyone's doing it these days anyway.

252
00:15:50,115 --> 00:15:52,076
There's an additional stipulation.

253
00:15:55,412 --> 00:15:58,374
I have the option of doing
any surgery I want.

254
00:16:02,795 --> 00:16:04,004
You know Wonjae Hospital, right?

255
00:16:04,088 --> 00:16:05,255
PRIORITIZE DR. GYE'S PREFERENCES

256
00:16:05,339 --> 00:16:07,007
We got a call from there the other day.

257
00:16:07,091 --> 00:16:09,426
Seems the word has spread
about our Dr. Gye all the way there.

258
00:16:10,469 --> 00:16:14,848
My melons are such high-end produce,
and so difficult to come by.

259
00:16:15,975 --> 00:16:18,185
I wonder if I need to keep more on hand?

260
00:16:22,898 --> 00:16:24,316
PATIENTS' RIGHTS AND RESPONSIBILITIES

261
00:16:24,400 --> 00:16:26,276
WE WILL NOT APOLOGIZE TO PATIENTS

262
00:16:32,950 --> 00:16:34,368
DOCTORS' STRIKE: OUR FIGHT HAS JUST BEGUN

263
00:16:39,498 --> 00:16:41,834
<i>Dr. Hwang in neurosurgery is sick.</i>

264
00:16:41,917 --> 00:16:44,962
But the problem is,
there's no one to operate on him.

265
00:16:45,045 --> 00:16:45,879
Who?

266
00:16:45,963 --> 00:16:48,090
The one who was gone
at the same time as Dr. Jang.

267
00:16:48,173 --> 00:16:50,467
Remember, that doctor
you said you'd make him quit?

268
00:16:50,551 --> 00:16:52,636
- Oh.
- Well, it's not just general surgery.

269
00:16:52,720 --> 00:16:55,097
Surgeries are being canceled everywhere.
It's total chaos.

270
00:16:55,180 --> 00:16:57,641
Oh, I'm not sure if the food's
going in my mouth or my nose.

271
00:16:57,725 --> 00:16:59,268
It's going in your mouth.

272
00:16:59,351 --> 00:17:02,896
Yeah, yeah, make sure to eat up.
So you can do lots of surgeries.

273
00:17:03,897 --> 00:17:05,524
Hey, stop requesting me, would you?

274
00:17:05,607 --> 00:17:07,609
I'm tired of doing one surgery
after another.

275
00:17:07,693 --> 00:17:09,778
That reminds me,
could you open up an OR for me later?

276
00:17:09,862 --> 00:17:10,821
Okay. Send me an email request.

277
00:17:10,904 --> 00:17:15,075
Don't ask me in person.
I won't remember it. See you later.

278
00:17:19,204 --> 00:17:21,915
Uh, she's really busy
because there are so few doctors around.

279
00:17:21,999 --> 00:17:25,169
I thought anesthesiologists would
have it easier, but they don't seem to.

280
00:17:25,252 --> 00:17:29,923
Well, you must be pretty busy too, right?
So many co-workers have left.

281
00:17:30,883 --> 00:17:32,676
Oh! You…

282
00:17:37,306 --> 00:17:38,307
Uh…

283
00:17:40,726 --> 00:17:43,896
I was starting to wonder where they were.

284
00:17:46,398 --> 00:17:51,195
Dr. Ma's absence is really being felt. All
the patients seem pretty anxious lately.

285
00:17:56,867 --> 00:17:57,993
Yes, I'll make sure.

286
00:18:00,079 --> 00:18:02,581
Doctor, I'm afraid that your surgery

287
00:18:02,664 --> 00:18:04,291
will need to be canceled.

288
00:18:04,374 --> 00:18:06,585
There's no one available
to assist on that day.

289
00:18:08,378 --> 00:18:11,632
That's a bit harsh, Doctor,
don't you think? This is all because of--

290
00:18:12,257 --> 00:18:14,843
Hello? Hello?

291
00:18:16,095 --> 00:18:17,721
<i>We have more than enough ORs.</i>

292
00:18:17,805 --> 00:18:21,433
<i>But even if Dr. Jo opens up an OR,</i>
<i>there's no primary surgeon.</i>

293
00:18:21,517 --> 00:18:23,936
<i>And even if there is one,</i>
<i>there's no one to assist.</i>

294
00:18:24,019 --> 00:18:26,146
Of course there are no assistants.

295
00:18:26,230 --> 00:18:29,274
And they can't operate without one.
Or at least, they won't.

296
00:18:30,067 --> 00:18:30,901
Right.

297
00:18:30,984 --> 00:18:33,654
But you can learn a lot at times
like this, Dr. Tae-gyeong.

298
00:18:33,737 --> 00:18:36,740
You can watch and be part
of so many more surgeries

299
00:18:36,824 --> 00:18:38,826
than those interns in the cafeteria.

300
00:18:38,909 --> 00:18:41,745
But I'm not learning
much of anything right now.

301
00:18:41,829 --> 00:18:45,082
I'm just dealing with
the things that slip through the cracks.

302
00:18:45,165 --> 00:18:48,919
And the problem is
this work involves people's lives.

303
00:18:49,002 --> 00:18:52,464
So I'm really afraid
that I'm gonna miss something.

304
00:18:52,548 --> 00:18:55,801
It used to be that interns
never did this kind of work at all.

305
00:18:55,884 --> 00:18:58,428
Now, it's about all we do, these days.

306
00:18:58,512 --> 00:19:00,722
Oh, dear. Sorry about that.

307
00:19:06,270 --> 00:19:08,856
What was the point of building
a pediatric center?

308
00:19:08,939 --> 00:19:13,193
The OR situation over there was
like that even before the medical crisis.

309
00:19:13,986 --> 00:19:16,155
The ORs are there, but no surgeons.

310
00:19:16,238 --> 00:19:18,157
Oh, why'd they build it then?

311
00:19:18,240 --> 00:19:20,367
Reimbursement rates were so low

312
00:19:20,450 --> 00:19:23,245
that hospitals weren't prioritizing
pediatric surgeries,

313
00:19:23,328 --> 00:19:26,081
so the government raised the rates
to make them profitable.

314
00:19:26,165 --> 00:19:29,126
But it's a mess now
because they tried to rush everything.

315
00:19:30,085 --> 00:19:34,173
Hey, I bet you'll get a lot of consult
requests now, from the pediatric center.

316
00:19:35,424 --> 00:19:38,343
You're right, so that means…

317
00:19:38,427 --> 00:19:40,262
"You're right, so that means" what?

318
00:19:42,014 --> 00:19:44,474
Just stop thinking, okay?
Don't do anything.

319
00:19:44,558 --> 00:19:46,894
Just quietly perform
the surgeries that come in.

320
00:19:46,977 --> 00:19:49,229
"The option to do any surgery you want"?

321
00:19:49,313 --> 00:19:51,857
I put that in you contract in order
to boost your morale.

322
00:19:51,940 --> 00:19:54,067
I would've preferred to raise your fees.

323
00:19:54,151 --> 00:19:57,404
Would you stop thinking?
You're thinking, and I don't like it.

324
00:19:58,447 --> 00:20:02,075
Aren't pediatric surgery and adult surgery
totally different things, though?

325
00:20:02,159 --> 00:20:05,704
I heard you could crush a blood vessel
just by touching it too hard.

326
00:20:05,787 --> 00:20:07,873
That's why even expert surgeons
are reluctant,

327
00:20:07,956 --> 00:20:10,959
and the only ones who do them
are the pediatric specialists.

328
00:20:11,627 --> 00:20:13,212
They're just so small and fragile.

329
00:20:15,005 --> 00:20:19,218
Oh, Dr. Gye did an adorable
and truly admirable surgery today--

330
00:20:20,594 --> 00:20:22,471
You're busy. Get going.

331
00:20:22,554 --> 00:20:24,640
Quiet, before she smacks
the hell out of me

332
00:20:24,723 --> 00:20:26,475
for doing pro bono work, okay?

333
00:20:27,893 --> 00:20:30,020
Both those girls were raised
by their grandma?

334
00:20:30,103 --> 00:20:33,065
Oh, I wonder what she's sick with.

335
00:20:34,316 --> 00:20:36,109
She looks so pale, doesn't she?

336
00:20:36,193 --> 00:20:40,656
"Doc… tors'." "Doctors' walk…"

337
00:20:41,323 --> 00:20:43,158
- …out.
- "Walkout"?

338
00:20:43,992 --> 00:20:45,244
"Fi"?

339
00:20:45,327 --> 00:20:49,790
"Fight." Let's just go back
to my room and read a storybook.

340
00:20:49,873 --> 00:20:52,668
No, read the sign.

341
00:20:54,378 --> 00:20:59,216
"Begin a work stoppage."

342
00:20:59,800 --> 00:21:02,219
But what is that? What does it mean, huh?

343
00:21:03,095 --> 00:21:04,596
Let's go back now, okay?

344
00:21:04,680 --> 00:21:09,977
Stoppage! Walk out! Work stoppage!

345
00:21:10,060 --> 00:21:14,398
- Quiet!
- Doctors' walkout! Work stoppage!

346
00:21:14,481 --> 00:21:16,066
- Stop it right now.
- You stop!

347
00:21:21,196 --> 00:21:27,035
My puppy, my calf, my kitty.

348
00:21:27,119 --> 00:21:30,247
Ga-eul, my beautiful baby.

349
00:21:31,123 --> 00:21:32,624
Me too, me too!

350
00:21:34,001 --> 00:21:37,963
Ga-yeong, my beautiful baby.

351
00:21:38,046 --> 00:21:41,425
My kitty, my calf,

352
00:21:41,508 --> 00:21:45,429
my puppy.

353
00:21:54,146 --> 00:21:55,981
Yoo Ga-eul, ten years old.

354
00:21:56,064 --> 00:21:59,318
After a needle biopsy, she was diagnosed
with ganglioneuroblastoma.

355
00:21:59,401 --> 00:22:02,571
It is located in the retroperitoneal
space, encasing the aorta,

356
00:22:02,654 --> 00:22:03,947
and the inferior vena cava,

357
00:22:04,031 --> 00:22:07,034
as well as the right renal artery
and vein and ureter.

358
00:22:07,117 --> 00:22:10,287
Why are you requesting a consultation
for a benign tumor?

359
00:22:10,370 --> 00:22:11,496
I see it's quite extensive.

360
00:22:11,580 --> 00:22:13,832
Well, because
clinically it's neuroblastoma.

361
00:22:14,708 --> 00:22:16,585
She completed eight cycles of chemo,

362
00:22:16,668 --> 00:22:18,712
but there was no decrease in size.

363
00:22:19,338 --> 00:22:21,882
Ganglioneuroblastoma…

364
00:22:21,965 --> 00:22:24,718
It's clear from the imaging that the tumor
in the spinal canal

365
00:22:24,801 --> 00:22:28,764
is affecting the surrounding organs,
so surgery is absolutely necessary.

366
00:22:28,847 --> 00:22:31,808
It was scheduled for tomorrow. But…

367
00:22:31,892 --> 00:22:34,144
since the pediatric center
is so understaffed,

368
00:22:34,227 --> 00:22:36,229
we requested a consult from NS and GS.

369
00:22:36,313 --> 00:22:39,232
She's gotta be in pain right now.

370
00:22:39,316 --> 00:22:41,276
But shouldn't we operate
as soon as we can?

371
00:22:41,360 --> 00:22:43,528
Obviously.
But that's not an option right now,

372
00:22:43,612 --> 00:22:44,988
so they're passing the buck around.

373
00:22:45,072 --> 00:22:47,407
Which seems to be the purpose
of today's meeting.

374
00:22:48,325 --> 00:22:50,494
When was the surgery rescheduled for?

375
00:22:50,577 --> 00:22:54,790
Well, we haven't yet.
We don't have a surgeon or assistants.

376
00:22:54,873 --> 00:22:58,126
We looked into transferring her,
but everyone is reluctant,

377
00:22:58,210 --> 00:23:00,796
since the surgery is extensive
and requires collaboration.

378
00:23:02,005 --> 00:23:06,176
Director, they put out an order.
The government will take legal action

379
00:23:06,259 --> 00:23:09,346
against any medical professional
participating in the strike.

380
00:23:10,889 --> 00:23:11,973
In other words,

381
00:23:13,850 --> 00:23:15,602
medical licenses
are going to get revoked--

382
00:23:15,685 --> 00:23:16,728
What?

383
00:23:16,812 --> 00:23:20,982
Are they crazy? That'll only make
more of them leave! Come on, why?

384
00:23:26,988 --> 00:23:29,324
DR. MA SEONG-GYU

385
00:23:35,622 --> 00:23:37,707
DR. BAE HEUNG-GON

386
00:23:40,961 --> 00:23:42,504
I don't know, it's just terrible.

387
00:23:43,130 --> 00:23:44,464
Come on.

388
00:23:45,298 --> 00:23:47,175
He always picks up when I call.

389
00:23:48,969 --> 00:23:50,345
He's doing it on purpose, isn't he?

390
00:23:50,429 --> 00:23:54,015
Um, let's pause the conference for now.
Given what's happening--

391
00:23:54,099 --> 00:23:55,016
No, no, we can't.

392
00:24:00,897 --> 00:24:03,859
Uh… Uh, I-I mean,

393
00:24:04,860 --> 00:24:06,903
what about the state of the patient?

394
00:24:06,987 --> 00:24:09,531
MOLLY GOES SHOPPING

395
00:24:09,614 --> 00:24:11,616
<i>How much longer is</i>
<i>she supposed to hold out?</i>

396
00:24:13,076 --> 00:24:15,328
38 HOURS BEFORE WORK STOPPAGE

397
00:24:15,412 --> 00:24:16,580
Please.

398
00:24:17,372 --> 00:24:20,125
Won't you please, Nurse,
can you do something for us?

399
00:24:20,876 --> 00:24:23,879
I'm sorry, ma'am. I'm so sorry.

400
00:24:28,550 --> 00:24:33,680
Then tell me, what are
we supposed to do? Where do we go?

401
00:24:38,810 --> 00:24:40,270
I'm so sorry, ma'am.

402
00:24:56,328 --> 00:24:57,787
Oh, goodness…

403
00:24:58,413 --> 00:25:03,126
My puppy… my kitty…

404
00:25:04,294 --> 00:25:11,259
my calf, my chick, my bunny.

405
00:25:24,481 --> 00:25:25,649
Mom…

406
00:25:28,109 --> 00:25:29,528
Papa…

407
00:25:32,447 --> 00:25:33,657
I'll stay

408
00:25:34,699 --> 00:25:37,244
a little bit longer and then I'll come.

409
00:25:40,330 --> 00:25:41,623
Please help me.

410
00:25:43,833 --> 00:25:47,504
Who's going to look
after Ga-yeong and Grandma?

411
00:25:49,714 --> 00:25:52,968
Help me. Help me.

412
00:25:59,391 --> 00:26:02,227
Should I go to the pediatric center?
Which room is it?

413
00:26:02,310 --> 00:26:05,313
- Dr. Gye, what are you doing?
- Gye Su-jeong, sit down.

414
00:26:07,524 --> 00:26:08,608
Sit down.

415
00:26:09,859 --> 00:26:11,444
Gye Su-jeong!

416
00:26:11,528 --> 00:26:14,948
Uh, she probably won't sit down
unless she has a snack in her hand.

417
00:26:15,031 --> 00:26:16,783
You want me to shoot you
with a tranquilizer?

418
00:26:16,866 --> 00:26:20,287
Either explain yourself and get outta
here, or shut up and sit down.

419
00:26:23,039 --> 00:26:28,044
I'm allowing you to perform any surgery
you want. Is now a good time for that?

420
00:26:30,255 --> 00:26:33,925
But we don't have anyone to assist.
An OR and a primary surgeon's not enough.

421
00:26:34,009 --> 00:26:35,135
It is enough.

422
00:26:35,218 --> 00:26:37,596
- What?
- I know exactly how I'm gonna do it.

423
00:26:38,221 --> 00:26:40,599
Are you planning to do a solo surgery?

424
00:26:40,682 --> 00:26:42,517
SOLO SURGERY: PRIMARY SURGEON
OPERATING WITHOUT AN ASSISTANT

425
00:26:45,145 --> 00:26:46,021
Looks like it.

426
00:26:46,855 --> 00:26:49,941
From the hospital's standpoint, though,
we can't let you perform

427
00:26:50,025 --> 00:26:53,653
what's already a difficult surgery
by yourself without any assistants.

428
00:26:53,737 --> 00:26:56,406
Even if you're board-certified,
you can't just push ahead like this.

429
00:26:56,489 --> 00:26:58,241
What will you do
when something goes wrong?

430
00:26:58,325 --> 00:27:01,453
Then… when's it gonna be done?

431
00:27:02,871 --> 00:27:05,749
Wait for someone to be available,
coordinate the timing with them.

432
00:27:05,832 --> 00:27:07,584
But if we can't get an OR,
it all falls through.

433
00:27:07,667 --> 00:27:09,336
So when's it going to be?

434
00:27:09,419 --> 00:27:10,670
Not one of you wants to make time,

435
00:27:10,754 --> 00:27:12,881
so stop striking for a minute
and assist me in this.

436
00:27:12,964 --> 00:27:14,132
Still, what you're asking is--

437
00:27:14,215 --> 00:27:18,553
Ever been kicked in the stomach? Ever had
your stomach crushed under a huge rock?

438
00:27:18,637 --> 00:27:22,891
Right now, as we're speaking, a
ten-year-old's getting her stomach kicked.

439
00:27:22,974 --> 00:27:26,561
It's like someone has placed a huge rock
on her stomach.

440
00:27:26,645 --> 00:27:29,773
If you're not going to remove it,
if you won't help her,

441
00:27:29,856 --> 00:27:31,733
be decent enough to look the other way.

442
00:27:34,402 --> 00:27:38,865
We're all doctors here. And as doctors,
we can't just look the other way.

443
00:27:38,948 --> 00:27:40,325
Then assist me, Doctor.

444
00:27:44,579 --> 00:27:45,747
If you are a doctor,

445
00:27:47,040 --> 00:27:48,124
then help with the surgery.

446
00:28:00,762 --> 00:28:02,931
She's the only doctor
who's not on strike at the moment.

447
00:28:03,014 --> 00:28:05,684
She'll be a replacement
for the time being.

448
00:28:05,767 --> 00:28:08,937
Right now, public opinion
and the online forums are looking bad.

449
00:28:12,482 --> 00:28:13,566
When will you operate?

450
00:28:14,192 --> 00:28:16,903
As originally scheduled, tomorrow, 12 p.m.

451
00:28:17,696 --> 00:28:20,073
Tomorrow, tomorrow? Day after today?

452
00:28:20,615 --> 00:28:24,285
We completed all the tests,
so we can keep to the schedule, right?

453
00:28:26,746 --> 00:28:31,251
I have another surgery to do. This one's
gonna go over ten hours. I can't make it.

454
00:28:32,669 --> 00:28:35,714
Six hours. I'll make it work.

455
00:28:35,797 --> 00:28:37,006
Wow, wow.

456
00:28:38,216 --> 00:28:39,342
Dr. Gye.

457
00:28:42,929 --> 00:28:46,433
If you finish this surgery in six hours,
and it's successful,

458
00:28:47,308 --> 00:28:52,522
I will broaden the scope
of that clause in your contract.

459
00:28:58,403 --> 00:29:00,739
You could just do it now…

460
00:29:02,198 --> 00:29:03,450
because I never fail.

461
00:29:07,746 --> 00:29:09,372
I'll tell Ms. Jang what you said.

462
00:29:25,889 --> 00:29:28,057
I'm going to contact urology
and ask them to put in double-J stents.

463
00:29:28,141 --> 00:29:29,934
Oh, I'll make that call.

464
00:29:30,018 --> 00:29:32,437
I have other work I have to do
around that time, otherwise I would help.

465
00:29:32,520 --> 00:29:35,023
Those who are of no help
should stay out of the way.

466
00:29:36,107 --> 00:29:38,568
You didn't hurt my feelings.
I know it's the truth.

467
00:29:39,903 --> 00:29:41,362
I'm just glad she's getting the surgery.

468
00:29:42,614 --> 00:29:43,990
So what's the game plan here?

469
00:29:44,657 --> 00:29:47,494
Open the abdomen, locate the tumor,
identify the major vessels,

470
00:29:47,577 --> 00:29:49,245
and take it out as cleanly as possible.

471
00:29:49,329 --> 00:29:51,915
With the double-J stent in place,
the ureter should be fine.

472
00:29:51,998 --> 00:29:54,626
Do a frozen biopsy
from around the vessels and ureter.

473
00:29:54,709 --> 00:29:57,045
If we confirm the tumor is benign,
close her up temporarily--

474
00:29:57,128 --> 00:29:59,005
Close her up temporarily,
move on to the spine,

475
00:29:59,714 --> 00:30:01,132
and apply Ioban.

476
00:30:01,216 --> 00:30:04,427
Flip her into the prone position,
proceed with spinal canal mass excision.

477
00:30:04,511 --> 00:30:05,470
Are you assisting?

478
00:30:06,638 --> 00:30:10,391
I have another surgery. If it weren't
for Dr. Gye, it would've been on my plate.

479
00:30:12,060 --> 00:30:14,354
To tell the truth,
I don't know if I could do it.

480
00:30:14,437 --> 00:30:18,066
It feels like I would tear those
tiny blood vessels if I even touched them.

481
00:30:18,149 --> 00:30:20,902
I don't even know if it's feasible,
actually. I got worried.

482
00:30:22,529 --> 00:30:24,364
Before I knew it, I was out here.

483
00:30:25,365 --> 00:30:28,952
You know, both her parents died
in a hit-and-run accident,

484
00:30:29,035 --> 00:30:31,037
so her grandmother's been collecting
scrap paper--

485
00:30:31,120 --> 00:30:33,081
Wait, how do you know all that, Doctor?

486
00:30:33,164 --> 00:30:36,626
The accident happened
during the strike of 2020.

487
00:30:36,709 --> 00:30:38,962
They got sent from one ER to another…

488
00:30:40,129 --> 00:30:43,341
It was in the news.
Both had severe abdominal bleeding,

489
00:30:43,424 --> 00:30:46,135
and by the time I saw them,
well, it was already too late.

490
00:30:46,803 --> 00:30:50,723
Of course Kim Seong-jin would take them.
But does anyone else know?

491
00:30:50,807 --> 00:30:54,686
Dr. Do knows too. That's why
he accepted my consult request.

492
00:30:54,769 --> 00:30:57,021
Her parents died because of the strike,

493
00:30:57,105 --> 00:30:59,566
now she might die too
because of another strike?

494
00:30:59,649 --> 00:31:01,067
Why'd you put it like that?

495
00:31:01,150 --> 00:31:04,153
You know it's not that simple,
so why say it that way?

496
00:31:04,237 --> 00:31:05,989
She didn't lose her parents
'cause of the strike.

497
00:31:06,072 --> 00:31:09,367
That's true.
It wasn't because of the strike.

498
00:31:12,036 --> 00:31:14,497
"I will practice my profession
with conscience and dignity."

499
00:31:14,581 --> 00:31:15,456
We all promise that.

500
00:31:16,958 --> 00:31:19,252
Conscience and dignity were both missing.

501
00:31:20,086 --> 00:31:23,047
That is why her parents died that day.

502
00:31:32,974 --> 00:31:35,351
<i>It's incredibly painful to stand by</i>

503
00:31:35,435 --> 00:31:37,020
<i>and watch the media and the public</i>

504
00:31:37,103 --> 00:31:39,355
<i>diminish this collective action</i>

505
00:31:39,439 --> 00:31:44,569
<i>to a simple matter of doctors' arrogance</i>
<i>and residents' selfishness.</i>

506
00:31:44,652 --> 00:31:46,487
<i>We're the ones asking</i>
<i>the difficult question</i>

507
00:31:46,571 --> 00:31:49,532
<i>of who really forced doctors</i>
<i>to leave their patients' sides.</i>

508
00:31:50,450 --> 00:31:53,244
<i>Half of the residents at</i>
<i>Guseo University Seonam Medical Center</i>

509
00:31:53,328 --> 00:31:57,790
<i>have already handed in their resignations</i>
<i>and begun a work stoppage…</i>

510
00:31:57,874 --> 00:32:00,126
I just don't get
how they can fight over their jobs

511
00:32:00,209 --> 00:32:01,961
when people's lives are at stake?

512
00:32:02,045 --> 00:32:03,254
Yeah, I know.

513
00:32:03,338 --> 00:32:07,800
The hospital told that woman next to us,
the breast cancer patient, to go home.

514
00:32:07,884 --> 00:32:09,594
Wasn't she here for chemotherapy?

515
00:32:09,677 --> 00:32:11,554
- Yeah, it's sad.
- My goodness.

516
00:32:11,638 --> 00:32:13,348
<i>They can't expect to have a conversation</i>

517
00:32:13,431 --> 00:32:15,642
<i>with doctors after such a coercive,</i>
<i>unilateral notice--</i>

518
00:32:23,483 --> 00:32:24,817
Dr. Gye Su-jeong.

519
00:32:27,278 --> 00:32:29,113
Oh.

520
00:32:30,365 --> 00:32:33,660
So the operation for Ms. Yu Ga-eul
is going forward as scheduled, I heard.

521
00:32:35,328 --> 00:32:37,163
And you're here
to tell her that, aren't you?

522
00:32:40,124 --> 00:32:44,671
Well, Dr. Jo was right. She said I'd
find you lurking out here in the hallway.

523
00:32:45,672 --> 00:32:46,965
"Lurking"?

524
00:32:47,048 --> 00:32:49,550
So she told me to do it instead.

525
00:32:52,762 --> 00:32:56,641
It's nice to know somebody's
getting their surgery on schedule.

526
00:32:59,185 --> 00:33:01,354
- Hello, ma'am.
- Oh, Nurse.

527
00:33:01,437 --> 00:33:04,065
You don't need to
worry about Ga-eul's surgery.

528
00:33:04,148 --> 00:33:07,276
My goodness! Thank you so much.

529
00:33:12,907 --> 00:33:15,034
- Careful, honey.
- You've been through a lot.

530
00:33:19,831 --> 00:33:21,541
- I'm so relieved.
- Hi, Hyeon-a.

531
00:33:21,624 --> 00:33:23,501
I'm gonna get the surgery.

532
00:33:23,584 --> 00:33:27,880
You're so lucky! My doctor
just disappeared all of a sudden.

533
00:33:27,964 --> 00:33:31,592
No.
He'll come back, okay? He'll come back.

534
00:33:31,676 --> 00:33:34,220
Yeah, he'll come back.
You'll be okay. You'll see.

535
00:33:34,303 --> 00:33:36,305
Ga-eul, what should we play?

536
00:33:36,389 --> 00:33:38,725
Hmm, let's draw together.

537
00:33:38,808 --> 00:33:41,227
- Okay.
- You wanna see my drawing?

538
00:33:41,310 --> 00:33:44,313
Wow! That looks great.

539
00:33:44,397 --> 00:33:47,358
Wow, my sister's really good at drawing.

540
00:33:50,278 --> 00:33:52,071
Neema.

541
00:33:52,155 --> 00:33:53,823
Yay!

542
00:34:02,165 --> 00:34:04,751
- That's her first doll.
- Mmm!

543
00:34:06,252 --> 00:34:08,212
Might be her last one, too.

544
00:34:19,682 --> 00:34:21,225
Okay…

545
00:34:31,277 --> 00:34:33,362
Here.

546
00:34:34,280 --> 00:34:37,867
Wow. She went through eight cycles of
chemo, and it hasn't shrunk much at all.

547
00:34:37,950 --> 00:34:40,661
That poor thing. She really suffered.

548
00:34:40,745 --> 00:34:43,623
Thank goodness
Su-jeong is going to ease her pain.

549
00:34:43,706 --> 00:34:46,125
Solo surgery should come
at a higher price, don't you think?

550
00:34:46,209 --> 00:34:48,544
Would you stop going on about money?

551
00:34:48,628 --> 00:34:51,422
- She's a child.
- All right, if you insist.

552
00:34:51,506 --> 00:34:53,841
The nerves posterior
to the transverse processes

553
00:34:53,925 --> 00:34:57,845
must be protected as much as possible,
since the tumor is mostly benign.

554
00:34:57,929 --> 00:34:59,931
- Mm-hmm.
- Yeah, don't damage the nerves.

555
00:35:00,014 --> 00:35:01,140
For the sake of her future.

556
00:35:04,143 --> 00:35:05,645
- There's more.
- Hmm?

557
00:35:05,728 --> 00:35:07,605
There are other charts you could look at.

558
00:35:07,688 --> 00:35:09,023
- I can hear you.
- There's lots of kids--

559
00:35:10,566 --> 00:35:12,276
But I won't do any of those.

560
00:35:19,117 --> 00:35:20,827
It only affects children, doesn't it?

561
00:35:20,910 --> 00:35:25,248
Yeah, it mostly just affects kids.
It's really rare, though.

562
00:35:25,331 --> 00:35:29,377
Whoa, that poor girl hung in there
for a long time. She's a tough cookie.

563
00:35:30,419 --> 00:35:31,712
Well done.

564
00:35:31,796 --> 00:35:32,630
YOO GA-EUL, F/10

565
00:35:34,382 --> 00:35:35,591
- Mi-gyeong.
- Hmm?

566
00:35:36,592 --> 00:35:38,386
Would you ever go back
to internal medicine?

567
00:35:38,469 --> 00:35:40,596
Or do you want to stay
in private practice?

568
00:35:48,688 --> 00:35:51,315
I thought that I'd be able
to save everyone, you know?

569
00:35:53,651 --> 00:35:55,194
When they would beg me to…

570
00:35:56,154 --> 00:36:00,074
let them go, 'cause it was just
too painful to go on, I'd get so angry.

571
00:36:00,783 --> 00:36:02,326
I couldn't accept it.

572
00:36:03,494 --> 00:36:08,124
"Why can't I save them?
Why are they in so much pain?"

573
00:36:08,207 --> 00:36:12,461
Even as I let them go with my own hands,
I never shed a tear.

574
00:36:12,545 --> 00:36:13,713
Wow…

575
00:36:14,297 --> 00:36:15,882
They'd be smiling, though.

576
00:36:18,217 --> 00:36:19,802
'Cause they weren't in pain.

577
00:36:23,097 --> 00:36:24,265
So…

578
00:36:25,683 --> 00:36:27,894
you save that little girl, Hmm?

579
00:36:35,902 --> 00:36:40,406
<i>The children must be in pain,</i>
<i>right? All the time.</i>

580
00:36:40,489 --> 00:36:43,993
Ga-eul. Are you in pain?

581
00:36:45,203 --> 00:36:46,913
Do you want me to call the doctor?

582
00:36:48,581 --> 00:36:49,582
No, it's okay.

583
00:36:50,166 --> 00:36:53,127
What are you doing here?
Can't sleep again?

584
00:36:53,211 --> 00:36:54,712
I wanted to give you this.

585
00:36:55,338 --> 00:36:58,883
When you're in pain, you can get a shot
that makes you feel better.

586
00:36:58,966 --> 00:37:01,677
Since you said it costs too much money,

587
00:37:02,720 --> 00:37:06,599
I gave you that to have
so you could get the shot.

588
00:37:06,682 --> 00:37:11,354
Thank you. But hey,
I won't need it, though.

589
00:37:11,437 --> 00:37:15,399
I just have to hold out a little longer,
'cause tomorrow I get my surgery done.

590
00:37:18,361 --> 00:37:21,155
But your surgery
could get rescheduled again.

591
00:37:22,156 --> 00:37:24,742
So many doctors keep disappearing
around here.

592
00:37:25,868 --> 00:37:30,498
This doctor won't disappear. The nurse
told me that she wasn't going to.

593
00:37:30,581 --> 00:37:33,584
Really? That's so great!

594
00:37:36,045 --> 00:37:38,881
<i>I hope tomorrow comes soon…</i>

595
00:37:39,632 --> 00:37:40,883
- I'm so happy.
<i>- …Mi-gyeong.</i>

596
00:37:54,522 --> 00:37:55,690
There it is.

597
00:38:14,166 --> 00:38:17,169
Is this… Snuggles?

598
00:38:21,299 --> 00:38:24,343
- <i>Dr. Gye. Dr. Gye.</i>
- <i>Dr. Gye.</i>

599
00:38:24,927 --> 00:38:26,095
- <i>Dr. Gye!</i>
- Dr. Gye!

600
00:38:30,933 --> 00:38:35,354
Come on, energy, get this person up. Hey--

601
00:38:41,193 --> 00:38:43,696
Okay sure, the ER may be closed
due to staff shortages,

602
00:38:43,779 --> 00:38:45,823
but what do you think you're doing?

603
00:38:45,906 --> 00:38:49,118
What, since we're closed, you own
the place now, do you? Huh?

604
00:38:49,201 --> 00:38:50,995
We'll open back up soon,
it's just a few days.

605
00:38:51,078 --> 00:38:55,666
The emergency room is closed?
Whoa, I had no idea.

606
00:38:56,917 --> 00:38:58,294
They put up a big sign out front.

607
00:38:59,170 --> 00:39:01,047
<i>Then again, you probably didn't see it.</i>
<i>Of course you didn't.</i>

608
00:39:01,130 --> 00:39:02,214
NOTICE OF EMERGENCY ROOM CLOSURE

609
00:39:04,300 --> 00:39:05,843
No patients since midnight last night.

610
00:39:07,136 --> 00:39:09,930
It's a first for me, too. Six years ago,
we stayed open during COVID.

611
00:39:10,806 --> 00:39:13,059
So far, 70% of the residents are gone.

612
00:39:14,643 --> 00:39:16,354
This is totally different from back then.

613
00:39:16,437 --> 00:39:17,396
Send them to me.

614
00:39:17,480 --> 00:39:19,315
What, are there ten more of you?

615
00:39:19,398 --> 00:39:20,399
You only need ten?

616
00:39:21,025 --> 00:39:24,779
Oh, Cat Feet, No Fun Won-jin.
By any chance, are you here for her?

617
00:39:24,862 --> 00:39:28,532
Well, you seem okay.
I thought you'd be ranting and raving.

618
00:39:28,616 --> 00:39:30,117
"You call yourselves doctors?"

619
00:39:30,201 --> 00:39:32,912
Then crying alone in some corner,
saying, "I'm sorry."

620
00:39:33,954 --> 00:39:38,167
Me? No, no, no. No way.

621
00:39:38,250 --> 00:39:40,795
- Where are you going?
- Damn it…

622
00:39:42,880 --> 00:39:45,216
How can you do this, huh?
You call yourselves doctors?

623
00:39:45,299 --> 00:39:51,138
I'm sorry.
I couldn't stop them from closing the ER.

624
00:39:53,933 --> 00:39:58,562
What? No, I'm absolutely fine. I got
a good night's sleep, so I feel great.

625
00:40:01,273 --> 00:40:03,109
Is it a transfer?
Is it a call about a transfer?

626
00:40:03,192 --> 00:40:07,405
He slept so good, his eyes are bloodshot.
Hey, what are you doing here again?

627
00:40:07,488 --> 00:40:12,952
I just wanted tomorrow to come sooner.
So I came in early to wait.

628
00:40:13,035 --> 00:40:15,204
This is what happens
when you hang around Dr. Kim too much.

629
00:40:15,287 --> 00:40:17,915
Park Tae-gyeong too,
you're both so kind-hearted.

630
00:40:20,543 --> 00:40:22,086
- We don't have group rooms.
- Let's go.

631
00:40:22,169 --> 00:40:25,005
No, we don't have any rooms.
This isn't that kind of place. No.

632
00:40:26,549 --> 00:40:30,052
Hey, why do you look so cool?
You're just walking, but you look so cool.

633
00:40:30,136 --> 00:40:32,346
You guys look so cool
when you walk to surgery.

634
00:40:32,430 --> 00:40:37,017
I do too. I look so cool. "Suction."

635
00:40:41,605 --> 00:40:44,733
Oh, Dr. Ma!
What brings you to the staff room--

636
00:40:45,693 --> 00:40:49,822
Oh, uh, you're actually packing up, huh?
You're leaving the hospital?

637
00:40:49,905 --> 00:40:51,490
You're not, though, are you?

638
00:40:51,574 --> 00:40:53,284
Oh, no, I'm staying here.

639
00:40:53,993 --> 00:40:56,370
I wish there was some way
I could convince you to stay, too.

640
00:40:58,372 --> 00:40:59,290
Go back to work.

641
00:41:01,709 --> 00:41:04,795
You're getting double-boarded.
You can't spend all your time on this.

642
00:41:04,879 --> 00:41:08,174
Do you know how shocked your patients were
when they saw your interview yesterday?

643
00:41:08,257 --> 00:41:09,884
What was the point of all that?

644
00:41:10,843 --> 00:41:11,760
Huh?

645
00:41:11,844 --> 00:41:17,183
I spent so long working my ass off to get
double-boarded, and now, it's meaningless.

646
00:41:18,017 --> 00:41:20,436
They're saying they can
just hire more people to fill the gaps.

647
00:41:21,312 --> 00:41:24,940
I put in all those years of studying
and all that hard work

648
00:41:25,024 --> 00:41:27,151
just to get treated
like I'm nothing at all.

649
00:41:27,234 --> 00:41:30,446
Instead of supporting their staff
and trying get us to stay,

650
00:41:30,529 --> 00:41:32,698
they plan to replace us with new hires.

651
00:41:34,158 --> 00:41:35,493
What are we, machines?

652
00:41:36,410 --> 00:41:37,828
Look, Dr. Ma…

653
00:41:40,039 --> 00:41:43,751
Oh, uh… Here, it's the book you loaned me.

654
00:41:43,834 --> 00:41:48,797
- Whatever, keep it.
- No, you have to read it again. Okay?

655
00:41:50,299 --> 00:41:53,636
Hey, what are you doing?
Move so Dr. Ma can leave.

656
00:42:18,536 --> 00:42:20,287
EMERGENCY RESPONSE COMMITTEE MEETING
ON URGENT MATTER

657
00:42:20,371 --> 00:42:21,664
AGENDA: INTERN AND RESIDENT STRIKE VOTE

658
00:42:21,747 --> 00:42:26,252
You're doing this in person?
It should be done online, shouldn't it?

659
00:42:26,335 --> 00:42:28,671
If we don't see their faces,
we can't weed them out.

660
00:42:28,754 --> 00:42:30,464
If they don't show up, they're traitors.

661
00:42:30,548 --> 00:42:31,674
What kind of vote is that?

662
00:42:31,757 --> 00:42:36,804
I knew you wouldn't come. Your father runs
a hospital, so this doesn't matter to you?

663
00:42:40,599 --> 00:42:42,810
No, it doesn't matter to me.

664
00:42:42,893 --> 00:42:44,728
Can you believe
the way this bastard talks?

665
00:42:44,812 --> 00:42:48,107
- Hey, why did you come here?
- What?

666
00:42:48,190 --> 00:42:50,234
I mean, you went to Yeongsin University.

667
00:42:50,985 --> 00:42:53,320
And we know, Yeongsin is
a much more prestigious school

668
00:42:53,404 --> 00:42:55,072
than this little backwater university.

669
00:42:55,906 --> 00:42:57,074
And it's a branch hospital, too.

670
00:42:57,157 --> 00:42:59,743
Don't you think you're being
a little too self-deprecating?

671
00:42:59,827 --> 00:43:02,997
I mean, Park Tae-gyeong, it's not like
you caused any trouble there.

672
00:43:03,080 --> 00:43:06,083
Why'd you ditch such a good place
and come all the way here?

673
00:43:06,166 --> 00:43:07,209
Did you dig up dirt on me?

674
00:43:07,293 --> 00:43:10,129
This is a small field.
I didn't have to dig much.

675
00:43:10,796 --> 00:43:13,132
Out of the 140,000 doctors in Korea,

676
00:43:13,215 --> 00:43:15,259
there are only about
8,000 interns and residents.

677
00:43:15,342 --> 00:43:16,927
And those 8,000 are the ones

678
00:43:17,011 --> 00:43:19,346
who keep all
the university hospitals in Korea running.

679
00:43:19,430 --> 00:43:23,058
And then we got stabbed in the back
while we were getting worked to the bone.

680
00:43:23,142 --> 00:43:26,895
But out of all those 8,000 people,
you're one of our biggest traitors.

681
00:43:26,979 --> 00:43:28,981
Why'd you come to our school
just to betray us?

682
00:43:29,064 --> 00:43:30,983
You'll drop
our participation rate, damn it.

683
00:43:31,066 --> 00:43:33,277
I told you, it's because
his dad's a hospital director,

684
00:43:33,360 --> 00:43:34,653
you selfish son of a bitch.

685
00:43:38,907 --> 00:43:39,825
Hey.

686
00:43:40,701 --> 00:43:42,786
Is there anyone here
who's not a damn doctor?

687
00:43:45,039 --> 00:43:47,958
I mean, anyone who's not a doctor's son?

688
00:43:49,084 --> 00:43:52,379
Your dad's an ophthalmologist.
Your mom's a dermatologist.

689
00:43:52,463 --> 00:43:53,297
And you…

690
00:43:54,590 --> 00:43:57,718
isn't your dad a vet? That would
explain your inferiority complex.

691
00:43:57,801 --> 00:43:58,677
Listen, you little--

692
00:43:58,761 --> 00:44:00,679
I asked if there's anyone here
who's not a damn doctor.

693
00:44:01,722 --> 00:44:04,475
Hey, anyone here become a doctor
'cause you were poor?

694
00:44:05,768 --> 00:44:08,145
Or because you wanted to save lives?

695
00:44:08,228 --> 00:44:11,440
You assholes are rich and your degrees
were handed to you.

696
00:44:11,523 --> 00:44:14,151
The only reason
you became doctors was to get richer,

697
00:44:14,234 --> 00:44:17,655
now you're about to put your patients'
lives on the line and walk out.

698
00:44:17,738 --> 00:44:19,990
How can you brand those
who stay behind as traitors,

699
00:44:20,074 --> 00:44:23,619
just because they wanna care
for their patients? Hey.

700
00:44:25,120 --> 00:44:25,996
Hey.

701
00:44:26,997 --> 00:44:31,835
It's you assholes, who're the selfish
ones. Where'd your conscience go, huh?

702
00:44:31,919 --> 00:44:34,004
All this from a lackey
for some temp doctor outta nowhere--

703
00:44:34,088 --> 00:44:34,922
What did you say?

704
00:44:35,005 --> 00:44:36,674
- What do you think you're doing?
- Say it again!

705
00:44:37,800 --> 00:44:38,676
Park Tae-gyeong.

706
00:44:42,137 --> 00:44:43,347
Should I call Dr. Gye?

707
00:44:44,390 --> 00:44:46,058
You wanna face the disciplinary committee?

708
00:45:01,407 --> 00:45:06,995
Let him go. Or else, I'll send you
to Dr. Kim Seong-jin. As a patient.

709
00:45:15,504 --> 00:45:17,256
Now. Hit him, Park Tae-gyeong!

710
00:45:17,339 --> 00:45:20,259
What are you talking about?
You guys, get out.

711
00:45:24,680 --> 00:45:27,349
Hey, you. What's the rush?

712
00:45:27,433 --> 00:45:30,352
Don't you still owe an apology
to our temp and her lackey?

713
00:45:39,069 --> 00:45:40,988
You could've stopped it. You were here.
Why didn't you?

714
00:45:41,071 --> 00:45:45,367
You could've stopped it. You were
right outside. Why didn't you?

715
00:45:45,451 --> 00:45:46,410
Ow!

716
00:45:47,327 --> 00:45:49,538
I was listening
because it sounded interesting,

717
00:45:49,621 --> 00:45:53,083
and then, Park Tae-gyeong
transformed into someone else.

718
00:45:54,042 --> 00:45:54,960
I'm sorry.

719
00:45:55,043 --> 00:45:56,545
Why are you sorry?

720
00:45:56,628 --> 00:45:58,130
Well, if I hadn't said anything--

721
00:45:58,213 --> 00:45:59,673
You're from Yeongsin University?

722
00:46:01,008 --> 00:46:03,135
Most of your colleagues went to Guseo,

723
00:46:03,218 --> 00:46:06,221
and they don't like outsiders,
so now I get why you don't have friends.

724
00:46:07,389 --> 00:46:08,432
I'm sorry.

725
00:46:09,975 --> 00:46:11,268
What for?

726
00:46:16,982 --> 00:46:20,944
Why did you come to Guseo? You must've
known what the hierarchy is like here.

727
00:46:21,028 --> 00:46:25,449
Oh, I don't know.
I just wanted to try a different school.

728
00:46:25,532 --> 00:46:29,620
Really? Just 'cause?
That's the best you could do?

729
00:46:29,703 --> 00:46:31,455
Oh, wait, you have a surgery this morning.

730
00:46:31,538 --> 00:46:33,582
- It's over.
- Oh…

731
00:46:34,416 --> 00:46:36,668
I wanted to nap beforehand.

732
00:46:37,336 --> 00:46:38,253
We gotta go.

733
00:46:54,436 --> 00:46:56,188
MOM

734
00:47:03,195 --> 00:47:05,948
Ms. Yoo Ga-eul's surgery
is at 12:00, right?

735
00:47:12,287 --> 00:47:16,583
You know, even though her sister's name
means autumn, she wasn't born in the fall.

736
00:47:18,085 --> 00:47:20,254
Her grandmother gave her that name.

737
00:47:20,796 --> 00:47:23,048
She's been poor her whole life,

738
00:47:23,131 --> 00:47:26,635
and she wanted her granddaughter's life
to be bountiful, like the season.

739
00:47:26,718 --> 00:47:29,972
After the accident,
their mother lived only a few days.

740
00:47:32,015 --> 00:47:35,602
The grandmother would visit with Ga-yeong
on her back and holding Ga-eul's hand.

741
00:47:43,235 --> 00:47:44,903
Are you sure you can do this by yourself?

742
00:47:45,779 --> 00:47:47,573
I was mistaken.

743
00:47:47,656 --> 00:47:51,243
You're better off without
that superficial conscience and dignity.

744
00:47:52,077 --> 00:47:54,621
What I mean is, you can't afford to fail.

745
00:47:55,289 --> 00:47:56,790
Can any of us afford to fail?

746
00:48:01,003 --> 00:48:02,462
Hey, Gye Su-jeong!

747
00:48:06,133 --> 00:48:10,637
Dr. Bae, me, Director Bu,
we've all failed before.

748
00:48:10,721 --> 00:48:12,848
Every doctor has failed at least once.

749
00:48:13,682 --> 00:48:16,685
That's why they break down,
and that's why they want compensation.

750
00:48:17,311 --> 00:48:20,147
That's why they go on strike,
and that's why they walk out!

751
00:48:21,481 --> 00:48:23,191
Because the fear of failure is intense,

752
00:48:25,152 --> 00:48:27,237
and the consequences are horrifying.

753
00:48:27,863 --> 00:48:31,450
So how can you talk
about failure so dismissively,

754
00:48:31,533 --> 00:48:35,829
and go around saying that
you won't ever fail? You're a doctor!

755
00:48:42,711 --> 00:48:43,921
Dr. Do Yun-sik.

756
00:48:46,256 --> 00:48:49,426
Do you know what the biggest difference is
between you and me?

757
00:48:51,845 --> 00:48:55,515
It's that I don't want to fail,
so I do it myself,

758
00:48:55,599 --> 00:49:00,687
but you, you don't want to fail,
so you just avoid it.

759
00:49:05,150 --> 00:49:06,276
We'll have to…

760
00:49:06,944 --> 00:49:08,278
close him back up.

761
00:49:08,362 --> 00:49:11,698
Dr. Do. Is your plan
really just to give up trying?

762
00:49:12,991 --> 00:49:15,369
Wouldn't it be better if you could say

763
00:49:15,452 --> 00:49:18,747
you did everything you possibly could
until the very end?

764
00:49:18,830 --> 00:49:20,082
I do not fail

765
00:49:21,249 --> 00:49:24,252
simply because I must not fail.

766
00:49:37,849 --> 00:49:39,267
The camera has been set up.

767
00:49:40,102 --> 00:49:41,144
Let's begin.

768
00:49:52,447 --> 00:49:53,615
Harmonic.

769
00:50:07,421 --> 00:50:12,426
<i>I do not fail simply</i>
<i>because I must not fail.</i>

770
00:50:18,390 --> 00:50:19,766
Let's begin the time-out.

771
00:50:24,688 --> 00:50:26,273
Okay, let's begin.

772
00:50:28,358 --> 00:50:29,735
Let's do a time-out.

773
00:50:30,902 --> 00:50:32,779
What is the patient's registration number?

774
00:50:35,115 --> 00:50:38,243
2-0-2-6…0-0-7…

775
00:50:38,326 --> 00:50:40,746
Whoa! Dr. Hwang! Dr. Hwang!

776
00:50:40,829 --> 00:50:43,248
Are you okay?
Doctor, call for help! Hurry!

777
00:50:43,331 --> 00:50:46,168
<i>The government is issuing</i>
<i>a nationwide return-to-work order</i>

778
00:50:46,251 --> 00:50:49,629
<i>to all resident doctors</i>
<i>at all hospitals, effective immediately.</i>

779
00:50:50,297 --> 00:50:54,051
<i>Violation of this order will result in</i>
<i>the revocation of your medical license</i>

780
00:50:54,134 --> 00:50:56,803
<i>and will also subject you</i>
<i>to legal sanctions.</i>

781
00:50:56,887 --> 00:50:59,931
<i>Furthermore, a separate</i>
<i>return-to-work order will be issued,</i>

782
00:51:00,015 --> 00:51:02,726
<i>which is in accordance with Article 59</i>
<i>of the Medical Service Act…</i>

783
00:51:04,936 --> 00:51:08,940
Hwang, Hwang! Stay with us! Hwang!

784
00:51:09,024 --> 00:51:11,026
Geez, what's going on?

785
00:51:11,109 --> 00:51:15,238
Who's the patient? What surgery is this?
Put up that CT scan. How far did he get?

786
00:51:15,322 --> 00:51:18,742
<i>Medical personnel must not, without</i>
<i>just cause, collectively or individually…</i>

787
00:51:18,825 --> 00:51:21,036
Oh, they've gone absolutely crazy, huh?

788
00:51:21,119 --> 00:51:23,955
What are they gonna do,
throw us doctors in jail?

789
00:51:25,165 --> 00:51:27,375
<i>To personnel or the head of</i>
<i>a medical institution…</i>

790
00:51:27,459 --> 00:51:30,504
Are you seeing this, Dr. Ma?
Why don't you come to the office?

791
00:51:31,213 --> 00:51:33,215
Seriously, a return-to-work order?

792
00:51:33,298 --> 00:51:35,759
Actually sounds just like forced labor,
doesn't it? Huh?

793
00:51:36,718 --> 00:51:39,012
If they push too hard, the residents are…

794
00:51:39,513 --> 00:51:41,556
It's also the medical students
who are opposed.

795
00:51:41,640 --> 00:51:44,851
Oh, of course. Kids these days hate
that sort of thing!

796
00:51:44,935 --> 00:51:46,895
Hey, this isn't a curse,
more like an opportunity.

797
00:51:46,978 --> 00:51:48,814
They'll see what happens
when there's no more doctors.

798
00:51:48,897 --> 00:51:50,565
It'll be a wake up call.

799
00:51:50,649 --> 00:51:53,902
If any patient happens to be harmed as
a result of the strike,

800
00:51:53,985 --> 00:51:57,405
it would mean that the doctor
is the one who'd be liable.

801
00:51:57,489 --> 00:51:59,658
Oh, you wanna make
problems here, Director Bu?

802
00:51:59,741 --> 00:52:01,701
That wake up call you said you wanted,

803
00:52:02,369 --> 00:52:05,247
if they got it, it could easily result
in lawsuits being filed.

804
00:52:05,330 --> 00:52:08,875
Well, damn it, Director Bu! Are you going
to just keep giving us more bad news?

805
00:52:08,959 --> 00:52:10,293
There was a particular incident

806
00:52:10,377 --> 00:52:13,088
which I believe happened
during the strike of 2000.

807
00:52:13,171 --> 00:52:16,007
A four-year-old was brought
to the ER, but because of the strike,

808
00:52:16,091 --> 00:52:18,051
the child couldn't get a surgery
that was needed

809
00:52:18,135 --> 00:52:20,220
and the child's condition got worse.

810
00:52:20,303 --> 00:52:25,016
The parents sued and the hospital was
ordered to pay 300 million won in damages.

811
00:52:25,851 --> 00:52:29,146
As doctors, you should remember that.

812
00:52:44,327 --> 00:52:45,912
Long time no see, Dr. Ma.

813
00:52:49,833 --> 00:52:52,043
Are preparations going well?

814
00:52:54,963 --> 00:52:56,047
I'm doing my best.

815
00:52:57,883 --> 00:52:58,800
Dr. Ma Seong-gyu.

816
00:52:58,884 --> 00:53:03,805
Director. Dr. Hwang Min-gu
collapsed in the OR during surgery.

817
00:53:09,728 --> 00:53:11,646
- Thanks for your hard work!
- Good work.

818
00:53:11,730 --> 00:53:12,814
Good work.

819
00:53:19,988 --> 00:53:22,657
Dr. Hwang's surgery was scheduled,
for the day after tomorrow,

820
00:53:22,741 --> 00:53:23,783
but it got postponed.

821
00:53:23,867 --> 00:53:27,996
He said he was feeling fine,
and insisted on performing his surgeries.

822
00:53:28,079 --> 00:53:29,372
He said that, as a patient,

823
00:53:29,456 --> 00:53:32,792
he realized just how upsetting it is
to have your surgery postponed.

824
00:53:32,876 --> 00:53:34,294
Dr. Hwang? That doesn't sound like him.

825
00:53:34,377 --> 00:53:36,046
Actually, his work ethic is quite strong.

826
00:53:36,129 --> 00:53:38,924
When it comes to performing surgeries,
he gives it his all.

827
00:53:39,007 --> 00:53:42,302
The problem, is that,
he's a patient himself now…

828
00:53:52,145 --> 00:53:55,065
Dr. Kim. Uh, Dr. Hwang is here, right?

829
00:53:55,148 --> 00:53:56,775
Yeah, he just went up to the OR.

830
00:53:56,858 --> 00:54:00,862
For surgery? Who's doing it?
We don't have a GS available right now…

831
00:54:02,239 --> 00:54:03,281
Oh, is it Bae Heung-gon?

832
00:54:04,157 --> 00:54:07,077
Oh, Dr. Do. Where's Dr. Hwang?

833
00:54:20,882 --> 00:54:25,637
She's going to do a laparoscopic
procedure all by herself? This is crazy.

834
00:54:27,347 --> 00:54:31,226
I've only seen a laparoscopic caudate
lobectomy done by a single surgeon

835
00:54:31,309 --> 00:54:33,520
once before at Johns Hopkins University.

836
00:54:34,187 --> 00:54:35,146
This is incredible.

837
00:54:36,690 --> 00:54:38,900
There's probably only a few surgeons
in the country who can do that.

838
00:54:38,984 --> 00:54:44,447
I believe Dr. Gye is currently
demonstrating that she's one of those few.

839
00:54:48,076 --> 00:54:51,579
Dr. Gye, what about
Ms. Yoo Ga-eul's surgery at 12:00?

840
00:54:51,663 --> 00:54:55,250
12:00? It's already just past 11:00.

841
00:54:55,333 --> 00:54:56,876
That's why I'm doing it laparoscopically.

842
00:54:56,960 --> 00:54:59,212
She says she can make it to
the surgery at 12:00.

843
00:55:03,717 --> 00:55:05,010
You could postpone if you need to.

844
00:55:05,093 --> 00:55:07,095
No. I'll make it no matter what.

845
00:55:07,929 --> 00:55:10,390
I won't let her be in pain
for even a minute longer.

846
00:55:17,355 --> 00:55:21,609
Come on. Just a little faster.

847
00:55:23,153 --> 00:55:24,404
A little faster.

848
00:55:38,710 --> 00:55:40,211
I think she's actually gonna make it.

849
00:55:41,254 --> 00:55:42,380
Sure looks like it.

850
00:55:44,007 --> 00:55:44,841
Thank goodness for that.

851
00:55:47,302 --> 00:55:50,972
- I have to get ready for my surgery.
- I need to go to mine, too.

852
00:56:05,820 --> 00:56:06,654
Dr. Bae.

853
00:56:07,697 --> 00:56:08,698
Yes?

854
00:56:09,991 --> 00:56:10,909
Do you think…

855
00:56:13,244 --> 00:56:14,996
we failed, you and I?

856
00:56:18,500 --> 00:56:19,709
What are you talking about?

857
00:56:20,335 --> 00:56:23,797
I'm talking about our mad dog in there,
who's surgery-obsessed.

858
00:56:23,880 --> 00:56:27,050
Who grabs a laparoscope
and uses it completely alone,

859
00:56:28,051 --> 00:56:30,428
doing a complex surgery
in an OR that's empty

860
00:56:30,512 --> 00:56:33,598
all because there's no one around
to assist her.

861
00:56:35,892 --> 00:56:39,687
You know, today, I realized,
she's not obsessed with surgery.

862
00:56:40,438 --> 00:56:42,857
She's obsessed with saving people's lives.

863
00:56:47,987 --> 00:56:48,947
So we're the losers.

864
00:56:51,741 --> 00:56:54,702
In comparison,
this strike suddenly feels so trivial.

865
00:56:59,124 --> 00:57:01,376
It might end sooner than we thought.

866
00:57:01,459 --> 00:57:06,047
I mean, she could even get to eat
a sandwich before her next surgery begins.

867
00:57:11,052 --> 00:57:12,512
Seong-gyu, uh…

868
00:57:14,514 --> 00:57:15,807
wasn't there.

869
00:57:15,890 --> 00:57:18,601
Oh, uh, he's with
Chairman Kim and Mayor Im--

870
00:57:18,685 --> 00:57:22,605
I'm in favor of the strike.
I support them. Only…

871
00:57:23,857 --> 00:57:29,154
Seong-gyu should know that I support it,
though. I need to show him that I do.

872
00:57:29,696 --> 00:57:34,534
It would really help him a lot if he could
just see that. I think that…

873
00:57:36,035 --> 00:57:39,456
I think that he might be missing
all the important moments in this thing.

874
00:57:43,543 --> 00:57:46,379
25 HOURS BEFORE WORK STOPPAGE

875
00:57:46,463 --> 00:57:48,840
2026 INTERN AND RESIDENT
EMERGENCY RESPONSE COMMITTEE MEETING

876
00:57:50,216 --> 00:57:51,968
Uh, as soon as you see the reporters…

877
00:57:52,051 --> 00:57:54,179
- Make it good, 'cause I'm watching you.
- Yeah, okay, okay, okay.

878
00:57:54,262 --> 00:57:55,763
Hey, we're good. Get up there already.

879
00:57:55,847 --> 00:57:57,223
Okay, I'll go and…

880
00:58:03,938 --> 00:58:08,026
When you're asleep, if Mommy and Daddy
show up in your dreams,

881
00:58:08,109 --> 00:58:11,446
don't follow them anywhere, okay?
Understand?

882
00:58:13,823 --> 00:58:16,659
Still, though,
it sure would be nice to say hi.

883
00:58:18,786 --> 00:58:23,249
Ga-eul, if you meet Mommy and Daddy,
tell them I want a visit, too.

884
00:58:23,875 --> 00:58:28,880
And tell them that they have to say,
"I'm Mommy" and "I'm Daddy,"

885
00:58:28,963 --> 00:58:31,633
'cause I don't remember
a whole lot about them.

886
00:58:32,467 --> 00:58:33,801
Okay, you got it.

887
00:58:49,192 --> 00:58:50,818
You have 22 minutes remaining.

888
00:59:01,204 --> 00:59:02,789
Just a little more…

889
00:59:27,605 --> 00:59:32,610
Uh, hey-- Hey, good work. Good work.

890
00:59:45,331 --> 00:59:46,916
ENERGY DRINK

891
00:59:51,212 --> 00:59:54,299
Every university hospital
has a statue like this.

892
00:59:55,425 --> 00:59:57,927
People take pictures in front of it
when they're starting school.

893
00:59:58,011 --> 01:00:00,471
Well, the statue here is pretty big.

894
01:00:04,809 --> 01:00:08,479
There's a surgeon called "Doctor X."

895
01:00:10,315 --> 01:00:11,316
Sorry?

896
01:00:11,399 --> 01:00:13,693
Dr. Bae and Dr. Ma found an article

897
01:00:13,776 --> 01:00:17,196
while looking for Mr. Park Gwang-cheol's
surgical records,

898
01:00:18,781 --> 01:00:22,744
which said that Doctor X was the surgeon
who had performed that same surgery.

899
01:00:23,411 --> 01:00:28,249
Oh. Is that so? Well, it's a big world,

900
01:00:28,333 --> 01:00:31,919
there are all kinds of surgeries,
and there are a lot of doctors, too.

901
01:00:32,545 --> 01:00:33,963
I didn't believe it.

902
01:00:34,589 --> 01:00:37,759
Of course you didn't. How could you
believe a silly rumor like that?

903
01:00:37,842 --> 01:00:40,970
But after watching the surgery
she did today,

904
01:00:41,054 --> 01:00:43,348
I thought, "Perhaps it's a possibility."

905
01:00:45,558 --> 01:00:47,310
What are you driving at, Director?

906
01:00:50,271 --> 01:00:53,941
<i>Dr. Gye is the same age as Dr. Ma.</i>

907
01:00:54,025 --> 01:00:56,819
At that age,
having that level of surgical skill,

908
01:00:56,903 --> 01:00:59,572
and performing surgeries
with all her energy--

909
01:00:59,656 --> 01:01:04,535
Director, Dr. Gye is a genius,
but in order to get this far,

910
01:01:04,619 --> 01:01:07,038
she's had to put in
a tremendous amount of effort.

911
01:01:07,121 --> 01:01:10,917
I'm a little disappointed you have
such misconceptions about her.

912
01:01:13,378 --> 01:01:18,841
At a time when this statue of Hippocrates
and the Hippocratic Oath

913
01:01:18,925 --> 01:01:23,262
are merely used as backdrops for photos
or a scene of a strike,

914
01:01:23,346 --> 01:01:27,058
I can't help but wonder,
"Who is Dr. Gye Su-jeong, really?"

915
01:01:31,771 --> 01:01:34,774
I don't wanna hear any more of this.

916
01:01:34,857 --> 01:01:36,859
The surgery will be starting soon.
Excuse me.

917
01:01:37,485 --> 01:01:38,569
Are…

918
01:01:40,405 --> 01:01:41,572
Gye Su-jeong…

919
01:01:59,090 --> 01:02:00,842
Let's begin the surgery.

920
01:02:06,180 --> 01:02:07,849
OPERATION TIME, TIME, ANESTHESIA TIME

921
01:02:08,850 --> 01:02:10,476
<i>Are Gye Su-jeong…</i>

922
01:02:13,271 --> 01:02:16,357
and Doctor X the same person?

923
01:03:00,151 --> 01:03:03,112
DOCTOR X: MAFIA IN WHITE

924
01:03:42,235 --> 01:03:45,196
DOCTOR X: MAFIA IN WHITE

925
01:03:45,279 --> 01:03:48,032
<i>We should just wash</i>
<i>our hands of this hospital.</i>

926
01:03:48,115 --> 01:03:49,492
<i>I have to do this surgery.</i>

927
01:03:49,575 --> 01:03:52,912
<i>No, you can't. That'll make you</i>
<i>even more like Doctor X.</i>

928
01:03:52,995 --> 01:03:54,789
<i>I'm telling you,</i>
<i>there is no surgical method.</i>

929
01:03:54,872 --> 01:03:56,874
<i>The child doesn't have much time.</i>

930
01:03:56,958 --> 01:03:59,710
Are you saying
you'll put patients' lives at risk

931
01:03:59,794 --> 01:04:01,879
to derail other people's careers?

932
01:04:01,963 --> 01:04:04,423
I'm saying I want to save
the life of an eight-year-old patient.

933
01:04:04,507 --> 01:04:07,468
<i>If you do that surgery,</i>
<i>you really will be fired.</i>

934
01:04:07,552 --> 01:04:09,387
<i>Do you think anyone will participate?</i>

935
01:04:09,470 --> 01:04:10,888
I'm begging you.
